  // sys_mmap(addr_hint, length, prot, flags) -> mapped VA or negative errno.
  //
  // Deliberately 4-arg (anonymous-mapping shape only: addr_hint,
  // length, prot, flags) rather than POSIX's full 6-arg (..., fd,
  // offset) form -- this kernel has no VMA-backed-file mapping
  // substrate yet (no page-cache-to-VMA wiring exists in core/mm/),
  // so a fd-backed mmap has no body to call even at the floor-landing
  // stage. A future fd-backed extension would need its own sysno
  // (arity 6 pushes into the two-move-shuffle family sys_mount/sys_
  // sendto already use) rather than widening this one in place.
